        as an Intangible Cultural Heritage.
    - time: 16.304
      text: To the Betawi people, a golok is never just a cutting tool, but a symbol
        of courage, honor, and the duty to protect one's family.
  - key: sarung_simpay
    title:
      id: Sarung Tanduk dan Simpay Kuningan
      en: Horn Sheath and Brass Bands
    text:
      id: Saat tersarung, keindahan golok tampak dari sarung tanduk kerbau belang
        yang dipoles mengkilap. Empat belas lilitan simpay kuningan memeluk rapat
        seluruh batang sarung. Secara teknis, simpay mencegah sarung retak akibat
        benturan, sementara secara filosofis melambangkan ikatan persaudaraan yang
        kokoh.
      en: While sheathed, the golok displays its polished striated water-buffalo
        horn scabbard. Fourteen brass simpay bands wrap tightly along its entire
        body. Practically, these rings reinforce the sheath against splitting, while
        philosophically they symbolize the tight bonds of kinship and unity.
    stage: 0
    focusHotspot: simpay
    voiceID: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 88edd44220231fc4fb32af39158eeb78, type: 3}
    voiceEN: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4dbe353463000be45909dbb152ebafaf, type: 3}
    cuesID:
    - time: 0
      text: Saat tersarung, keindahan golok tampak dari sarung tanduk kerbau belang
        yang dipoles mengkilap.
    - time: 7.888
      text: Empat belas lilitan simpay kuningan memeluk rapat seluruh batang sarung.
    - time: 13.496
      text: Secara teknis, simpay mencegah sarung retak akibat benturan, sementara
        secara filosofis melambangkan ikatan persaudaraan yang kokoh.
    cuesEN:
    - time: 0
      text: While sheathed, the golok displays its polished striated water-buffalo
